    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d398">

                <pb facs="0932" n="892" sameAs="frus:frus1952-54v09p1/pg892"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">884A.00/2–852</note>
                <head>No. 398<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the President to the
                        Secretary of State</hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d398-f1"/></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1952-02-08">February 8, 1952</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>I understand that the tentative budget figures for Mutual Security for fiscal
                    year 1953 include the sum $25 million for Israel. I further understand that a
                    program for Israel aggregating about $80 million has been developed within the
                    Department of State. After considering the various aspects of the situation, I
                    believe that the program for Israel for fiscal year 1953 should total $80
                    million, and that the additonal $55 million should be in addition to the amounts
                    heretofore contemplated for economic aid.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Harry Truman</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d398-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d398-f1-content">
                <p>Addressed also to Director for Mutual Security Harriman and Director of the
                    Bureau of the Budget Lawton.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
